worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_17_yaw_aug_a6000_claude/plan_yaw_aug_a6000.md-129-- Five evaluation seeds quantify diffusion/evaluation variability, not training-seed variability. There is one training seed per arm.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_17_yaw_aug_a6000_claude/plan_yaw_aug_a6000.md-130-- Primary clean contrast: paired by evaluation seed, Yaw-Aug−P1 at 40k for each K/metric; directions follow metric arrows.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_17_yaw_aug_a6000_claude/plan_yaw_aug_a6000.md:131:- Secondary method contrast: Yaw-Aug−B-F, labelled architecture-vs-augmentation rather than a pure single delta.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_17_yaw_aug_a6000_claude/plan_yaw_aug_a6000.md:132:- Pre-registered regularization interpretation: improvement at yaw 0° is compatible with generic data-diversity regularization; evidence for yaw-specific learning requires substantially larger gains at 90°/180°/270° than at 0°. Do not attribute all rotated-input gains to learned yaw structure without this degradation-relative-to-0° analysis.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_17_yaw_aug_a6000_claude/plan_yaw_aug_a6000.md-133-- Robustness reports both absolute metrics by angle and degradation relative to each method's own 0° result.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_17_yaw_aug_a6000_claude/plan_yaw_aug_a6000.md-134-- Avoid claiming exact yaw invariance for Yaw-Aug; the test is empirical robustness/generalization.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_17_yaw_aug_a6000_claude/plan_yaw_aug_a6000.md:135:- **R1 — the regularization confound, registered before any Yaw-Aug metric is seen.** A yaw-augmented arm may beat the baselines on rotated inputs simply because random yaw increases effective data diversity (a generic regularizer), not because it learned anything yaw-specific. The 0° cells already collected in §6.1 are the discriminator, and the reading is fixed now: **pure regularization predicts a gain at 0° comparable to the gain at 90/180/270; yaw-specific learning predicts a much larger gain at the rotated angles than at 0°.** Report the 0° gain and the rotated gains side by side and state which pattern the data shows. Neither outcome is a failure — but the interpretation must not be chosen after seeing the numbers.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_17_yaw_aug_a6000_claude/plan_yaw_aug_a6000.md-136-- FD is reported but interpreted separately because prior FA results improve acoustic/retrieval metrics while FD can worsen.
worklog/worklog_yixun/exp_17_yaw_aug_a6000_claude/plan_yaw_aug_a6000.md-137-- The fixed endpoint, single training seed, source-generation difference, and checkpoint-band caveats are mandatory in the final analysis.
